{
  "info": {
    "name": "Template — Admin (S48–S50)",
    "description": "The admin spine on :3100 — 12-admin-console.md §3, §5.\n\n## Before you run it\n\n1. `openssl rand -base64 32` → `ADMIN_TOTP_ENC_KEY` in `backend/.env`. The admin process refuses to boot without it, on purpose.\n2. `cd backend && npm run db:reset` — **required**, see below.\n3. `cd backend && npm run dev:admin`\n\n## ★ Why this needs a fresh database every time\n\nEnrollment is deliberately once-only: `POST /auth/totp/enroll` refuses a second call with `ALREADY_ENROLLED`, because a silent re-enrollment would invalidate the authenticator the operator is holding. There is no API that creates an admin, so the collection cannot make itself a fresh one. Re-running against an already-enrolled admin fails at step 2, correctly.\n\nThat is also why this is a separate collection: the main one stays re-runnable and needs only `npm run dev`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "adminBaseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3100"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminApi",
      "value": "{{adminBaseUrl}}/admin/api/v1"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminEmail",
      "value": "admin@local.dev"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminPassword",
      "value": "change-me-before-prod"
    },
    {
      "key": "challengeId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "adminTotpSecret",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "adminTotpCode",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "adminUserId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "targetUserId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "auditLogId",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
